{
  "example": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`\n\nThis Bedrock configuration selects a model, AWS profile, and region for the\ndomain's cache:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::AgentConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::BedrockConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache;\n\nlet config = AgentConfig::Bedrock(\n    BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\".into())\n        .aws_profile(\"development\".into())\n        .region(\"us-east-1\".into()),\n);\nlet cache = ValidationCache::with_agent(config);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.setup` is a concrete case. It builds a Bedrock `AgentConfig` with model `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, AWS profile `development` and region `us-east-1`. It passes that config to `ValidationCache::with_agent` and expects the cache to select that agent. The cited requirements add three things. The cache starts empty. Backend setup is deferred. The SDK does not persist the configuration.\n\nThe one `{test}` reference to the example is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]`. It checks each outcome:\n- **Same inputs as the example:** the test builds the identical Bedrock config and calls `ValidationCache::with_agent(config.clone())`.\n- **Cache is empty and the agent is selected:** it asserts `outlines` is empty and `sources` is `None`. It asserts the cache holds an agent whose `config` equals the supplied Bedrock config. The clone-shared `Arc` pointer check (`Arc::ptr_eq`) shows the selection belongs to the domain's cache.\n- **Setup is deferred:** it runs `refresh_evidence` with the deterministic `Question(false)` criterion and gets a result without any Bedrock connection. The test does not check `provider.get().is_none()` itself. The sibling test `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` makes that assertion for OpenAI and also shows setup errors surface only on an awaited ask.\n- **Nothing is persisted:** it serializes the stored evidence record. It asserts there is no `backend` key and that the text contains neither `development` nor `claude-sonnet`.\n\nTest helpers (`TestDomain`, `Question`, `Content`) are simple and consistent with these assertions.\n\nUnresolved question: no assertion checks that the `BedrockConfig` builder methods store the profile and region. That belongs to the `BedrockConfig` and `agent_config` requirements, not to this example's attach-to-cache outcomes. Config equality in the test would catch `with_agent` altering or dropping the config. I found no gap.",
  "references": "7c7524ee8e51af918c33943dcb55e9936d8e326b278323071bdbeabdfe57c6a0",
